HYB T60_paperK: lqr_orig (paper K [-0.2562, -0.3031], dt 0.5 s) per controlled tenant, start target 24.66 % (T60); outer loop: hurt iff ratio < 0.94; (a) hurt + our drop within 2 s -> target / 0.8 up to ceiling 246.59 % (T600); (b) hurt + no drop of ours for 2 s -> donors (ratio > 1.0638, no SLO = inf, target <= base) x 0.8 down to floor 8.22 % (T20), at most once per 1 s; (c) hold 2 s, then back toward the base at 2.57 %/s, a raised target not below min(ceiling, CPU_eff + 16.44)
HYB NOTE: the ceiling 6 x cpu_ref (246.6 % of one core) is above the ~217 % needed to stop lqr_orig's 0.95 / 0 flip-flop on a victim (exp44: victims' u alternated on 100 % of S3 controller steps); a tenant whose target was raised and that has had no drop of ours for 2 s is flagged EXEMPT -- hyb then has learned to exempt it from lqr_orig, it is not tracking a CPU target; a tenant at the ceiling that is not exempt is still in the flip-flop
HYB NOTE: rule (b) is expected to be NEARLY A NO-OP: lqr_orig flip-flops, CPU_eff goes negative on the low half of the cycle, so u = 0 on every second step whatever the target; lowering a flooder's target cannot raise its duty cycle (exp44 S3: T40 vs T60 flooder totals 59.7 vs 60.1 Gbit/s). Cuts are logged (hyb_cuts, hyb_min_be_tgt), no effect on u is expected
LQR_ORIG (faithful port, exp43 code): per controlled tenant, dt 0.5 s = every 2nd 0.25 s tick, CPU = its vhost thread % of one core over that 0.5 s window (the SAME schedstat path for flooders and victims), median of last 5, CPU_eff = 0.7 smooth + 0.3 (smooth + trend), u = -K [e, edot], soft limit, clip [0, 0.95], nearest of 20 levels; actuator xdp_dropfrac.o swapped in on the controlled tenants for the slot and xdp_limit back on all six after it; PPS feed-forward and management-port exemption NOT enabled
DEVIATION (lqr_orig and hyb, documented): drop_bp -> 0 on every controlled tenant BEFORE waiting for the iperf3 clients, 60 s timeout + WARNING; S3: the victims' drop is released at t >= 40.5 s (end of the victim window, column victim_release_s; victim_win_after_release counts victims whose last SLO window ends after it)
S3 CHECK: V2's vhost CPU in each S3 reference must be >= 18.90 % of one core (1.15 x the T40 target 16.44 %) and every victim >= 0.97 x its offered rate (rep 1: refuse; later: WARNING)
TOKEN BUCKET: vfrot and lqr use xdp_limit.o on every flooder interface (burst 5 ms); victim interfaces xdp_limit, never limited (counter only), except under S3's lqr_orig
